\caption(Identity covariance does not distinguish an independent square from a dependent diamond.)
\alttext(Two four-point scatters show independent source corners and their rotated diamond. The table exposes every point and its squared coordinates. Printed correlations and joint/marginal zero counts verify nonlinear dependence exactly.)

>> A cubic update that can be checked by hand

For the independent corners and a unit direction \(w=(a,b)\), \(E[s_1^4]=E[s_2^4]=1\)
and mixed odd moments vanish. With the cubic contrast,
\(E[s(s^Tw)^3]-3w=(-2a^3,-2b^3)\). Starting at (.8,.6), the raw update is
(−1.024,−.432). After normalization, its direction ratio is
\((.6/.8)^3=.421875\). This exact example explains the locally cubic direction
convergence of the kurtosis update near a source axis; finite data and other
contrasts need their own analysis.

The same program fits ICA blindly to four mixtures with matrix rows (1,.6),(.3,1.2).
The native local-step call uses the already white source corners to verify the
hand calculation; the separate fitted model sees only the mixture columns. Its
diagnostics check whitening and reconstruction without treating either as a proof
that all possible source models have been identified.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ica_exact_update.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double> s(4, 2, {-1, -1, -1, 1, 1, -1, 1, 1});
  const auto                            step = dm::stats::ica_fixed_point_step(s, {.8, .6}, "cube");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame                d;
  d.add_column("x1", std::vector<double>{-1.6, -.4, .4, 1.6});
  d.add_column("x2", std::vector<double>{-1.5, .9, -.9, 1.5});
  const dm::stats::ICA m(d, {"x1", "x2"}, {2, "cube", 200, 1e-10, 7});
  auto                 left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  left.points(
          d.numeric_column("x1").values(),
          d.numeric_column("x2").values(),
          "mixture rows",
          {37, 99, 235},
          6)
      .title("The blind fit sees four mixtures")
      .x_label("x1")
      .y_label("x2")
      .x_limits(-2, 2)
      .y_limits(-2, 3);
  right.line({0, .8}, {0, .6}, "initial direction", {100, 116, 139})
      .line({0, -step.direction[0]}, {0, -step.direction[1]}, "updated", {220, 38, 38})
      .points({1}, {0}, "source axis", {37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .title("Cube update towards a source axis")
      .x_label("white coordinate 1")
      .y_label("white coordinate 2")
      .x_limits(-.1, 1.2)
      .y_limits(-.1, 1.5);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/ica_exact_update.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame::MarkdownOptions fmt;
  fmt.digits     = 9;
  fmt.scientific = {
      "whitening_error",
      "source_covariance_error",
      "rotation_error",
      "reconstruction_rmse",
      "alignment_error",
      "rank_threshold"};
  std::print(
      "Raw update: ({:.9f},{:.9f}); norm {:.9f}; direction ratio {:.9f}.\n\nBlind-fit "
      "diagnostics:\n\n{}\n\nPer-component status:\n\n{}\n\nFirst six completed updates:\n\n{}\n",
      step.raw_update[0],
      step.raw_update[1],
      step.update_norm,
      step.direction[1] / step.direction[0],
      m.diagnostics().to_md(fmt),
      m.component_diagnostics().to_md(fmt),
      m.convergence_history().head(6).to_md(fmt));
}
```
