\caption(Known independent non-Gaussian sources and Gaussian controls separate numerical stopping from identifiable source recovery.)
\alttext(For each of four data seeds and three contrast choices, two panels plot matched recovery and maximum iteration count for non-Gaussian and Gaussian families. All 24 fits appear in the table, including component-budget exhaustion; no significance comparison is inferred.)

All twelve non-Gaussian fits converge under the declared angle rule. Their mean
matched correlations range from .98948957 to .99985756. Seven of the twelve Gaussian
fits exhaust the 500-update budget; one of those still has mean matching .97614069.
A high score against an arbitrarily chosen Gaussian source basis therefore does not
resolve population nonidentifiability. The table keeps both the score and status.

>> Geometry and reconstruction answer different questions

Two independent uniform coordinates fill a square. The benchmark's mixing matrix
has rows (1,.8),(.3,1), producing a parallelogram. Plot the estimated mixing columns
from the two-component ICA fit in original feature units, alongside PCA's orthogonal
variance axes. The ICA columns may be oblique; its unmixing rows are their dual map.
All arrows below are rescaled for visibility and centred on the fitted mean.

Compare one-component and two-component ICA reconstructions. The one-component
model keeps only the leading PCA direction; rotating inside that retained
one-dimensional space cannot restore the discarded variation. Full two-component
reconstruction is nearly exact for any fitted orthogonal ICA rotation. The
retained variance and reconstruction table therefore verifies the fitted maps,
while only known-source matching evaluates separation here.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ica_geometry.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto                     d     = dm::stats::ica_benchmark(800, 7, "uniform");
  const std::vector<std::string> names = {"x1", "x2"};
  const dm::stats::ICA           full(d, names, {2, "logcosh", 500, 1e-8, 42}),
      reduced(d, names, {1, "logcosh", 500, 1e-8, 42});
  const dm::stats::PCA pca(d, names, {true, false});
  auto                 left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  left.points(
      d.numeric_column("x1").values(),
      d.numeric_column("x2").values(),
      "mixtures",
      {148, 163, 184},
      2);
  for (std::size_t c = 0; c < 2; ++c) {
    const double norm = std::hypot(full.mixing_matrix()(0, c), full.mixing_matrix()(1, c));
    left.line(
        {full.mean()[0] - 1.7 * full.mixing_matrix()(0, c) / norm,
         full.mean()[0] + 1.7 * full.mixing_matrix()(0, c) / norm},
        {full.mean()[1] - 1.7 * full.mixing_matrix()(1, c) / norm,
         full.mean()[1] + 1.7 * full.mixing_matrix()(1, c) / norm},
        c == 0 ? "ICA mixing columns" : "",
        {220, 38, 38});
    left.line(
        {full.mean()[0] - 1.7 * pca.loadings()(0, c), full.mean()[0] + 1.7 * pca.loadings()(0, c)},
        {full.mean()[1] - 1.7 * pca.loadings()(1, c), full.mean()[1] + 1.7 * pca.loadings()(1, c)},
        c == 0 ? "PCA axes" : "",
        {37, 99, 235});
  }
  const auto summary = reduced.diagnostics().concat_rows(full.diagnostics());
  left.title("Mixing patterns and variance axes")
      .x_label("mixture x1")
      .y_label("mixture x2")
      .x_limits(-3.5, 3.5)
      .y_limits(-3, 5.5);
  right
      .bars(
          {1, 2},
          summary.numeric_column("reconstruction_rmse").values(),
          "reconstruction RMSE",
          {37, 99, 235},
          .6)
      .title("Truncation discards a PCA direction")
      .x_label("retained component count")
      .y_label("RMSE per original-unit feature cell")
      .y_limits(0, .7);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/ica_geometry.svg");
  dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double> truth(d.nrows(), 2);
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < d.nrows(); ++i)
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < 2; ++j)
      truth(i, j) = d.double_at("s" + std::to_string(j + 1), i);
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame::MarkdownOptions fmt;
  fmt.digits     = 9;
  fmt.scientific = {
      "whitening_error",
      "source_covariance_error",
      "rotation_error",
      "reconstruction_rmse",
      "rank_threshold"};
  std::print(
      "Reconstruction checks:\n\n{}\n\nFull ICA source matching:\n\n{}\n",
      summary.to_md(fmt),
      dm::stats::ica_source_matches(truth, full.sources()).to_md(8));
}
