\caption(The mixing pattern is distinct from an unmixing covector, and exact reconstruction alone does not verify separation.)
\alttext(A uniform-mixture parallelogram is overlaid with red fitted mixing columns and blue PCA axes. A bar plot compares one- and two-component reconstruction RMSE. Tables give the numerical checks and supervised source matching for the full fit.)

> Iris: observed components without source truth

Iris has 150 flowers, four numeric measurements in centimetres and three species.
Fit all four measurement columns with logcosh, a 1000-update budget and 1e-7 angle
tolerance. No species label participates in centring, whitening or component extraction;
labels colour the scatter afterwards using the retained original-row map. Compare
retaining two and four PCA dimensions before ICA, and report every component's
numerical status and kurtosis.

These measurements are not supplied with a validated instantaneous independent-source
mixing model. Neither a visually separated species group nor non-Gaussian component
kurtosis establishes biological latent causes or independent sources. All rows are
used for this descriptive fit, with no classification accuracy or held-out prediction
claim. Full-rank reconstruction checks the linear algebra, while the reduced fit's
error records discarded variation. Both use frozen training means for later transforms.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ica_iris.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto                     d        = dm::datasets::iris();
  const std::vector<std::string> features = {
      "Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width", "Petal.Length", "Petal.Width"};
  const dm::stats::ICA full(d, features, {4, "logcosh", 1000, 1e-7, 42}),
      reduced(d, features, {2, "logcosh", 1000, 1e-7, 42});
  std::vector<std::string> groups;
  for (auto i : full.kept_row_indices())
    groups.push_back(d.string_at("Species", i));
  auto         left = full.plot_sources(groups), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const auto   y      = full.component(1);
  const auto   bounds = std::minmax_element(y.begin(), y.end());
  const double span   = *bounds.second - *bounds.first;
  left.title("Species labels added after fitting")
      .y_limits(*bounds.first - .1 * span, *bounds.second + .8 * span);
  const auto kurtosis = full.source_kurtosis();
  const auto k_bounds = std::minmax_element(kurtosis.begin(), kurtosis.end());
  right.bars({1, 2, 3, 4}, kurtosis, "excess kurtosis", {37, 99, 235}, .65)
      .title("Marginal shape is not independence")
      .x_label("component in extraction order")
      .y_label("empirical excess kurtosis")
      .y_limits(std::min(-.2, *k_bounds.first - .5), std::max(.2, *k_bounds.second + 2));
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/ica_iris.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame::MarkdownOptions fmt;
  fmt.digits     = 9;
  fmt.scientific = {
      "whitening_error",
      "source_covariance_error",
      "rotation_error",
      "reconstruction_rmse",
      "alignment_error",
      "rank_threshold"};
  std::print(
      "Data preview:\n\n{}\n\nTwo- and four-component checks:\n\n{}\n\nEvery component in the full "
      "fit:\n\n{}\n",
      d.head(4).to_md(2),
      reduced.diagnostics().concat_rows(full.diagnostics()).to_md(fmt),
      full.component_diagnostics().to_md(fmt));
}
```
